{"authored" [{"question" "q-33312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(3,2,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨2,2,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨3,2,2⟩,$ $n=⟨2,2,3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =⟨3,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6cfaac94bd0b4d595a377cd4441dbf9286c403902c2f3e6703575f61cf0f334c" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/