/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,2⟩=16"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨3,3,2⟩=4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(1,2,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6cfaac94bd0b4d595a377cd4441dbf9286c403902c2f3e6703575f61cf0f334c" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-9"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-1⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨3,2,1⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =⟨2,1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6cfaac94bd0b4d595a377cd4441dbf9286c403902c2f3e6703575f61cf0f334c" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨2,1,-1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=⟨1,1,1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨1,2,3⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨1,-1,2⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =⟨2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6cfaac94bd0b4d595a377cd4441dbf9286c403902c2f3e6703575f61cf0f334c" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=⟨2,1,-3⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=-5"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=⟨1,-1,2⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/state.json" "file_sha256" "04ef88cccb922c877c85c2641d3cc9562ebe95243c94b57280d25ec62e9cfa62" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(-3,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 0, 2, 0 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/example-4932.json" "file_sha256" "48f4f90a8b30b9d0b5794ce85853d58194d5a2a7b8ae3fde46d811c298cc0a79" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 0,2,0 \\rangle$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{r} - \\mathbf{p}) \\cdot \\mathbf{n} = 0,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $\\mathbf p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/example-4932.json" "file_sha256" "48f4f90a8b30b9d0b5794ce85853d58194d5a2a7b8ae3fde46d811c298cc0a79" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $\\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{b}, \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{c} \\rangle$ is parallel to the plane $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3.$ What is the value of $\\dfrac{b}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/example-4933.json" "file_sha256" "e0c18de60d0e06c0e252ff35465a6df0a54d5129950caa3d996d2269f76cff45" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4933" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t_1,t_2,t_3 \\rangle$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle.$ So, $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{n}$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\langle t_1, 2t_1 + 4t_3, t_3 \\rangle,\n$$\n\nwhere $t_1,t_3 \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $\\mathbf{v}$ equals $0.$ So, we must set $t_1=0.$ \n\nSince $\\mathbf{v}$ is nonzero, we can pick any $t_3 \\neq 0.$ For example, setting $t_3=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{4}, \\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{1} \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{b}{c} = 4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/example-4933.json" "file_sha256" "e0c18de60d0e06c0e252ff35465a6df0a54d5129950caa3d996d2269f76cff45" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(\\sqrt{2},0,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the line\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3 \\\\ y=-1+\\sqrt{3}t \\\\ z=5-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/example-4935.json" "file_sha256" "b912481a7fb121412248df876a4ba6cc934fc4ec1331f166c91dcccc0e13551d" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/assets/4c70e51d85874e5a241a5d9b35b147500d4c306187c5e0a1d15a48a9aef07706.png)\n\nThe direction vector of the line is $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1\\rangle,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =⟨\\sqrt{2},0,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/example-4935.json" "file_sha256" "b912481a7fb121412248df876a4ba6cc934fc4ec1331f166c91dcccc0e13551d" "basis" 1566 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-4,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-4,2⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,6,-4⟩-⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "af62567032904ab0c11d2f92c78708763fc073d35840b55f5e8617b45657faaf" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=⟨1,-4,2⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=-23"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,2⟩=⟨-1,5,-1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩=-23"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6{t}_{1}-2{t}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},3{t}_{1},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "af62567032904ab0c11d2f92c78708763fc073d35840b55f5e8617b45657faaf" "basis" 1722 "