/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4b9b06e7dbdb2611add074521225df3b7e3598baf948a597551507ef0424d01" "basis" 1722 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049832/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,-2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8b4058e6ad4d11c59444d5e560a5ee7d97491e0039706319ee0f41b2fbb700b" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.