/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(4,1,-3)$ and $B(7,-3,1)$, we can find a vector that is parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,-3,1⟩-⟨4,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨3,-4,4⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =⟨1,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩ & =23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8b4058e6ad4d11c59444d5e560a5ee7d97491e0039706319ee0f41b2fbb700b" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-4,-4,3⟩=11"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/140