/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨3,-4,4⟩=23"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-3,2,1)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-3,2,1⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,-2⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨6,-5,4⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8b4058e6ad4d11c59444d5e560a5ee7d97491e0039706319ee0f41b2fbb700b" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-5,6,4⟩=12"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-6,4,5⟩=28"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/m