loper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/state.json" "file_sha256" "c32c6a99e371d7454c830a8095a48f9fee7a3086ad669f98255dbdbd67457e9c" "basis" 2721 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14074013/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-32971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(2,-5,3)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨-1,2,-3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-32971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-5,3⟩,$ and $n=⟨-1,2,-3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ & =⟨2,-5,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩ & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-32971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-32971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-32971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩=-21"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩=-3"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩=⟨-2,5,-3⟩"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,-5,3⟩=21"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,-5,3⟩=⟨-1,2,-3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-32971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-3⟩=-21"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(3,2,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨2,2,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨3,2,2⟩,$ $n=⟨2,2,3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =⟨3,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=16"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,3⟩=4"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,3⟩=⟨3,2,2⟩"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,2⟩=16"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨3,3,2⟩=4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33312" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-4,5)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the position vector of $P$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane. \n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-70647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=9"] ["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=-11"] ["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=-20"] ["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=-11"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127632" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(\\sqrt{5},-1,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127632" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=\\sqrt{5}i-j+2k,$ and $n=\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k) & =(\\sqrt{5}i-j+2k)\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k) \\\\ r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k) & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127632" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-127632" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127632" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot (5i-3j+2k)=1"] ["math" "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i+2j-3k)=6"] ["math" "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k)=12"] ["math" "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k)=6"] ["math" "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-j-2k)=12"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127632" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot (\\sqrt{5}i-3j+2k)=12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(1,2,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-5"] ["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-9"] ["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9"] ["math" "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6{t}_{1}-2{t}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},3{t}_{1},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33319" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127911" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,2⟩=\\sqrt{11}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127911" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,2⟩=\\sqrt{11}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,2,2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}+2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{1} & =2{t}_{2}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨2{t}_{2}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{2},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{2},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨2,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127911" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-127911" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127911" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{11}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127911" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩=6$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-5,-1,4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -5{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},-5{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,-5,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=-\\frac{1}{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70822" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-70822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{4}"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70822" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,0,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨4,0,2⟩=16.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨4,0,2⟩=16$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨4,0,2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{3} & =-4{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{3} & =-2{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,-2{t}_{1}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the second component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{2}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{c}=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-33313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33313" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩=7$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,1,-2⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ -3{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-2{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127873" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨1,2,3⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨1,-1,2⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =⟨2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=0"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=⟨2,1,-3⟩"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=-5"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=⟨1,-1,2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-1⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨3,2,1⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =⟨2,1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=0"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨2,1,-1⟩"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=2"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=⟨1,1,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-70892" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-3,2,1)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-3,2,1⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+6t \\\\ y=3-5t \\\\ z=-2+4t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,-2⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨6,-5,4⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨6,-5,4⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩ & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-5,6,4⟩=12"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨-6,4,5⟩=28"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨4,-5,6⟩=-28"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩=-24"] ["math" "r\\cdot ⟨6,5,-4⟩=24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-127948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "r\\cdot ⟨6,-5,4⟩=-24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(1,-4,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨1,-4,2⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,-3)$ and $B(1,6,-4)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,6,-4⟩-⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,5,-1⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =⟨1,-4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,5,-1⟩ & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3772d6b854140e60bbd312b06204f6ca9a31bcadad5f7e63336617b8bfce89e"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "469aeca0be34dfbee839b187a5a6b65023627281cfe038dbd6e81074ac320b31"} {"question" "q-33317" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083941/state.json" "